{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:NuclearInteractions.CptOrbitClosureDensity","@type":"LeanModule","name":"NuclearInteractions.CptOrbitClosureDensity","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Real.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.List.Basic"],"declarations":15,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.CPTOrbit.ConditionalAudit.conditional_on_SymmetricCrystalPairProduction","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.CPTOrbit.ConditionalAudit.conditional_on_SymmetricCrystalPairProduction","kind":"theorem","line":196,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/nuclear-interactions/cpt-orbit-closure-density.lean#L196-L204","doc":"Witness theorem demonstrating the main proposition is conditional\non `[SymmetricCrystalPairProduction]` per CLAUDE.md §3b-cond:\nthe orbit-closure property is recovered directly from the class. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.CPTOrbit.ConditionalAudit.SymmetricCrystalPairProduction.pair_production","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.CPTOrbit.ConditionalAudit.SymmetricCrystalPairProduction.pair_production","kind":"theorem","line":191,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/nuclear-interactions/cpt-orbit-closure-density.lean#L191-L191","doc":"**The conjecture itself**: at every Hecke level `n`, every\npopulated Wedderburn-block list that is bar-invariant under the\nType-B fold (i.e. contains a partition iff it contains its\ntranspose) is CPT-saturated — chiral excitations occur only as\nbar-conjugate `σ`-pairs.  Stated in the shape of the claim\n(a fold-closure property), not as a bare `True`.  `sorry` in any\nconcrete instance is understood as conjecture per §3b. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.CPTOrbit.ConditionalAudit.SymmetricCrystalPairProduction.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.CPTOrbit.ConditionalAudit.SymmetricCrystalPairProduction.mk","kind":"ctor","line":183,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/nuclear-interactions/cpt-orbit-closure-density.lean#L183-L183","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.CPTOrbit.ConditionalAudit.SymmetricCrystalPairProduction","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.CPTOrbit.ConditionalAudit.SymmetricCrystalPairProduction","kind":"class","line":174,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/nuclear-interactions/cpt-orbit-closure-density.lean#L174-L194","doc":"Local stub of the conjecture's axiomatised class.  See the lake-\npackage sibling `QOU.BraidKnot.SymmetricCrystalPairProduction`\nfor the canonical declaration.\n\nEncodes the conjecture's content (Type-B fold-orbit closure):\nthe populated Wedderburn-block list of every baryon is closed\nunder the Type-B fold involution `σ = partitionTranspose`, so\nchiral excitations occur only as bar-conjugate pairs.  `sorry` in\nany concrete instance is understood as conjecture per §3b. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.cpt_orbit_closure_density_single_chirality","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.cpt_orbit_closure_density_single_chirality","kind":"theorem","line":133,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/nuclear-interactions/cpt-orbit-closure-density.lean#L133-L138","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.cpt_orbit_closure_density","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.cpt_orbit_closure_density","kind":"theorem","line":119,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/nuclear-interactions/cpt-orbit-closure-density.lean#L119-L131","doc":"**Main proposition**: ρ_F is determined by the orbit-closure\nstructure of the populated Wedderburn-block set under the\nType-B fold involution.\n\nNo Boolean is inserted by hand; the dichotomy\n`ρ_F ∈ {m_e, 2 m_e}` is a *consequence* of whether `Λ` is\ninvariant under `σ`. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:conj:cpt-orbit-closure-density","label":"conj:cpt-orbit-closure-density","md":"quantum-observable-universe/nuclear-interactions/cpt-orbit-closure-density.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.frobeniusPackingDensityValue","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.frobeniusPackingDensityValue","kind":"def","line":111,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/nuclear-interactions/cpt-orbit-closure-density.lean#L111-L117","doc":"Density value at the categorical scale `m_e`, parametrised by\nthe populated-blocks list.  Replaces\n`FrobeniusPackingDensity.value` from `mass-volume-factorization`,\nderiving the factor of 2 from the orbit-closure check. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.cpt_boolean_eq_orbit_closure","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.cpt_boolean_eq_orbit_closure","kind":"theorem","line":99,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/nuclear-interactions/cpt-orbit-closure-density.lean#L99-L109","doc":"**Boolean ↔ orbit-closure equivalence**.\n\nThe Frobenius packing density's `cptSaturated` Boolean equals\nthe decision procedure for `isCPTSaturated` on the populated-\nblocks list.  Hence the entire Boolean flag is structurally\ndetermined by the orbit structure of `Λ` under the Type-B\nfold — no per-link case analysis required. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.cptSaturatedBool","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.cptSaturatedBool","kind":"def","line":94,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/nuclear-interactions/cpt-orbit-closure-density.lean#L94-L97","doc":"Boolean form of the CPT predicate, matching the legacy\n`FrobeniusPackingDensity.cptSaturated` field. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.isCPTSaturated_decidable","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.isCPTSaturated_decidable","kind":"instance","line":82,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/nuclear-interactions/cpt-orbit-closure-density.lean#L82-L86","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.isCPTSaturated","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.isCPTSaturated","kind":"def","line":77,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/nuclear-interactions/cpt-orbit-closure-density.lean#L77-L80","doc":"A list of partitions is **CPT-saturated** iff it is closed\nunder the Type-B fold involution `σ`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.partitionTranspose_involutive","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.partitionTranspose_involutive","kind":"axiom","line":68,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/nuclear-interactions/cpt-orbit-closure-density.lean#L68-L71","doc":"`partitionTranspose` is involutive. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.partitionTranspose","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.partitionTranspose","kind":"def","line":53,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/nuclear-interactions/cpt-orbit-closure-density.lean#L53-L66","doc":"The Type-B fold involution: partition transpose `σ(λ) = λ^T`,\nthe Young-diagram conjugate.  Modelled here on the `List ℕ`\ncarrier as the column-length sequence\n`λ^T_j = #{ i : λ_i ≥ j }`; on a genuine (weakly-decreasing)\npartition it is the standard conjugate, identifying `(k) ↔ (1^k)`\nand acting as an involution (`partitionTranspose_involutive`).\nThe canonical construction is `YoungDiagram.transpose` in\nMathlib. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.partitionDecEq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.partitionDecEq","kind":"instance","line":47,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/nuclear-interactions/cpt-orbit-closure-density.lean#L47-L51","doc":"Decidable equality on partitions of `n` (inherited from the\n`List ℕ` carrier; the full structure reduces to `YoungDiagram`\ndecidability in Mathlib). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ParticleInteractions.Partition","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ParticleInteractions.Partition","kind":"def","line":42,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/nuclear-interactions/cpt-orbit-closure-density.lean#L42-L45","doc":"Abstract partition carrier (a lightweight stand-in for the full\n`Mathlib.Combinatorics.Young.YoungDiagram` structure: a partition\nof `n` is modelled here as its list of parts). ","signatureChunk":0}]}